    "teacher_markdown": "### **Walkthrough of Exemplar Code**\r\n\r\n#### **1. Selects the Button**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst buttonOne = document.getElementById(\"buttonOne\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis line finds the button in the HTML so the program can interact with it.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **2. Selects the Text Area**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nconst textArea = document.getElementById(\"textArea\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis selects the part of the page that will be updated.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **3. Adds an Event Listener**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\nbuttonOne.addEventListener(\"click\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis tells the program to listen for a click on the button.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **4. Event Handler (What Runs)**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n, () => {...}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis function contains the code that runs when the button is clicked.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n#### **5. Updates the Page (Response)**\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\ntextArea.textContent = \"Button One was clicked!\";\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis changes the text on the page when the button is clicked.\r\n"
